{"pin":"BH05894","subcodes":[{"code":"BH05894","anchor":"","first_line":"I know not, O my God, what the Fire is with which Thou didst light the Lamp of Thy Cause, or what the Glass","first_line_orig":"لم ادر یا الهی بای نار اوقدت سراج امرک و بای زجاجه حفظته من اعادی نفسک فو  ","language":"Ara","word_count":"170","full_text_parts":["I know not, O my God, what the Fire is which Thou didst kindle in Thy land.  Earth can never cloud its splendor, nor water quench its flame. All the peoples of the world are powerless to resist its force.  Great is the blessedness of him that hath drawn nigh unto it, and heard its roaring.\nSome, O my God, Thou didst, through Thy strengthening grace, enable to approach it, while others Thou didst keep back by reason of what their hands have wrought in Thy days.  Whoso hath hasted towards it and attained unto it hath, in his eagerness to gaze on Thy beauty, yielded his life in Thy path, and ascended unto Thee, wholly detached from aught else except Thyself.\nI beseech Thee, O my Lord, by this Fire which blazeth and rageth in the world of creation, to rend asunder the veils that have hindered me from appearing before the throne of Thy","majesty, and from standing at the door of Thy gate.  Do Thou ordain for me, O my Lord, every good thing Thou didst send down in Thy Book, and suffer me not to be far removed from the shelter of Thy mercy.\nPowerful art Thou to do what pleaseth Thee.  Thou art, verily, the All-Powerful, the Most Generous.","Do Thou preserve Thy loved ones, I beseech Thee, in the shelter of Thy shadowing mercy which transcendeth all things, that haply the sufferings they bear may not deter them from turning in the direction of Thy name, the All-Glorious, the Most Bountiful.”"],"translations":[{"language":"ru","lang_name":"Russian"},{"language":"es","lang_name":"Spanish"},{"language":"bg","lang_name":"Bulgarian"},{"language":"hi","lang_name":"Hindi"},{"language":"ro","lang_name":"Romanian"},{"language":"id","lang_name":"Indonesian"},{"language":"zh-Hant","lang_name":"Traditional Chinese"},{"language":"lb","lang_name":"Luxembourgish"},{"language":"sv","lang_name":"Swedish"},{"language":"tl","lang_name":"Tagalog"},{"language":"uk","lang_name":"Ukrainian"},{"language":"no","lang_name":"Norwegian"},{"language":"mt","lang_name":"Maltese"},{"language":"hy","lang_name":"Armenian"},{"language":"pt","lang_name":"Portuguese"},{"language":"da","lang_name":"Danish"},{"language":"fr","lang_name":"French"},{"language":"ky","lang_name":"Kirghiz"},{"language":"ta","lang_name":"Tamil"},{"language":"ko","lang_name":"Korean"},{"language":"af","lang_name":"Afrikaans"},{"language":"pl","lang_name":"Polish"},{"language":"ca","lang_name":"Catalan"},{"language":"en","lang_name":"English"},{"language":"el","lang_name":"Greek"},{"language":"tr","lang_name":"Turkish"},{"language":"is","lang_name":"Icelandic"},{"language":"az","lang_name":"Azerbaijani"},{"language":"it","lang_name":"Italian"},{"language":"de","lang_name":"German"},{"language":"lv","lang_name":"Latvian"},{"language":"sk","lang_name":"Slovak"},{"language":"nl","lang_name":"Dutch"},{"language":"tvl","lang_name":"Tuvalu"}],"writing_refs":[{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"ko","lang_name":"Korean"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"tr","lang_name":"Turkish"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"ta","lang_name":"Tamil"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"zh-Hant","lang_name":"Traditional Chinese"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"ro","lang_name":"Romanian"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"el","lang_name":"Greek"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"id","lang_name":"Indonesian"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"hy","lang_name":"Armenian"},{"type":"pm","type_name":"Prayers \u0026 Meditations","language":"fa"